title: '2026-11-15: the first-day reading is under "what I know"; these are the three changes I would make first.'
pid: dfdb5e70-575c-4a71-b2a4-897055f1b571
body: |2-
  What I am unsure of: the order of stops past the fourth is the order
  of the pages, not of anyone's trial, since nobody gets past the
  Docker step by reading alone; and four doubts are left for Cleo,
  Mario and Vic, as children of the reading. What surprised me: the
  pages most in Jeff's way of explaining ('vocabulary.org',
  'hyperlinks.org', 'data-model_friendly.org') are the ones the entry
  page links least or not at all. Tay should read the reordering of
  'docs/README.org' before Jeff does, since the meditation and the
  algebra are Jeff's own voice and the question is only where they
  sit. Once the first two changes are in, a fresh mind in a clean
  container, following 'docs/' alone, would test this better than a
  reading can.
contains:
